      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It mocks a `FailableRunnable` that does nothing (via `ViolatedAssumptionAnswer`), measures its execution duration with `DurationUtils.of()`, and verifies the result is not positive. I'll improve readability with better variable names and a clearer structure.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces the opaque auto-generated names (`failableRunnable0`, `duration0`, `boolean0`) with descriptive names (`noOpRunnable`, `measuredDuration`, `isPositive`) and adds a brief comment explaining why the duration is not positive — making the test's intent immediately clear without changing any runtime behaviour."
